      "content": "You raise a very valid concern, as curricula will inevitably reflect the courtesanisms of their creators rather than serving as neutral mirrors of history. However, it is academically unsound to present history as binary layers of \"true\" facts versus \"biased\" narratives, so avoiding hard truths on power dynamics actually results in a skewed educational experience. The most effective pedagogical approach is one that explicitly teaches students how to analyze competing historical accounts, rather than forcing them to choose between a safe, sanitized narrative and a contentious, activist-driven one.",
